.TH LUS-FMT 1 "" "Lus" "Lus Manual"
.SH NAME
lus-fmt \- format source files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBlus fmt\fR [\-\-check] [\-\-write] [\-\-strict] [\-\-indent N] [path ...]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Gives source files one standard layout.
With no option, it prints the formatted text of each file to standard output.
For a directory, it formats every \fB.lus\fR file inside it.
With no file, or with the file \fB\-\fR, it reads standard input.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-write\fR
Rewrite the files in place.
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fR
List the files that are not formatted and change nothing.
The exit status is 1 if the list has a file.
Use this option in continuous integration.
.TP
\fB\-\-strict\fR
Write the strict style, which \fBlus check \-\-strict\fR checks.
.TP
\fB\-\-indent N\fR
Use N spaces per indentation level.
The default is 4.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Every file was formatted, or with --check is formatted already.
.TP
1
A file would change or cannot be parsed.
.TP
2
An option is malformed or a file cannot be read or written.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lus (1)
.PP
The CLI page of the Lus manual, https://lus.dev/manual/cli#lus-fmt, has the same text with links to the rest of the manual.
